  "worked_solution": "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-\\frac{5}{y}+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-5{y}^{-1}+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =-5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-1})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =-5(-{y}^{-2})+2y \\\\  & =2y+5{y}^{-2} \\\\  & =2y+\\frac{5}{{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{y}^{3}+5}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2{y}^{3}+5}.\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $(-4,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(-4,1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{1}^{2}}{2(1)^{3}+5} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2+5} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point-slope formula for a tangent line, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-1 & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot (x-(-4)) \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{7}x+\\frac{4}{7}+1 \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{7}x+\\frac{11}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
